How to install the MicroEmacs on a BSD 4.1 System emulated by SimH:

(1) on your Linux Box:

    $ git clone https://github.com/JoachimSchneider/MicroEmacs
    $ git switch current
    $ cd MicroEmacs/ue500
    $ tar -H v7 -c -f /tmp/ue.tar h src cmd unx_anc
    $ gcc -o /tmp/simhtap ../tools/simhtap.c
    # Create a SimH format tape file
    $ /tmp/simhtap /tmp/ue.tar 20 > /tmp/ue.tar.tap

(2) We won't describe setting up BSD 4.1 in SimH here: There are
    several guides available in the net.

    Mount /tmp/ue.tar.tap as tape in SimH

(3) In BSD 4.1 (logged on as a non-root-user):

    We first build MicroEmacs

    $ cd
    $ mkdir UE
    $ cd UE
    $ tar xbf 20 /dev/rmt12
    $ cd unc_anc
    $ make -f makefile.bsd41 clean
    # This essentially calls `make -f makefile.bsd41' and filters out
    # those warnings which are expected. These warnings are caused e.g.
    # by the IS_ARRAY macro which uses the fact that for a C array
    # &array == &array[0].
    $ ./make_bsd41.sh

    Then we install it assuming that the current user is in the "users" group:

    $ su  root

    # mkdir           /usr/local
    # chgrp users /usr/local
    # chmod 0775 /usr/local
    # exit

    $ mkdir           /usr/local/pkg
    $ mkdir           /usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs
    $ mkdir           /usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs/bin
    $ mkdir           /usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs/cmd
    $ mkdir           /usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs/doc
    $ cp -p emacs     /usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs/bin
    $ cp -p .emacsrc  /usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs/bin/
    $ cd ../cmd/
    $ tar -cpf - . | (cd /usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs/cmd && tar -xpf -)

    $ cat runemacs
    #!/bin/sh -
    ## CHANGE THIS TO YOUR NEEDS:
    mybas=/usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs
    ##
    mybin="${mybas}/bin"
    mycmd="${mybas}/cmd"
    PATH="${mybin}:${mycmd}:${PATH}"
    export PATH
    exec "${mybin}/emacs" $@
    # EOF

    $ cp runemacs /usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs/bin/

    Then link /usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs/bin/runemacs to your prefered
    directory, e.g. ~/bin/ or /usr/bin (or /usr/local/bin). Yet no symbolic
    links on BSD 4.1:

    $ su root
    # ln /usr/local/pkg/MicroEmacs/bin/runemacs /usr/bin/uemacs
    # exit

    The file .emacsrc may be moved to your HOME directory.

(4) Done ... This document was written with MicroEmacs on BSD 4.1
    emulated by SimH.

    Joachim Schneider April 2025



